      "content": "# 33. Install, update, and import data sources\n\n_Part 4: Data sources, registries, and paths_\n\nAdd a datasource from a registry, update it within policy, or import a local package while retaining source and version evidence.\n\n## When to use this chapter\n\nUse installation commands after compatibility, registry trust, and package identity have been reviewed.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- A trusted package identifier or reviewed local artifact and explicit permission to install code.\n- Compatible core/runtime dependencies and any required native libraries.\n\n## Working method\n\n1. Choose an exact package identifier and, for reproducibility, \u0060--version\u0060. A registry \u0060--channel\u0060 selects a release stream rather than proving compatibility.\n2. \u0060data-sources import\u0060 accepts a reviewed local directory or ZIP; it is not an arbitrary remote URL downloader. Retain the artifact digest and source.\n3. Use \u0060--non-interactive --format json\u0060 in unattended install/import flows. Inspect installed metadata, then run a small query with the loaded schema before treating the update as successful.\n\n## Automation contract\n\nDo not advance a package train solely because installation succeeded; run a datasource-specific smoke query before continuing.\n\n## Verification\n\nRecord package version and digest, loaded schema, and one successful representative query.\n\n## Commands used\n\n- \u0060musoq data-sources install\u0060\n- \u0060musoq data-sources update\u0060\n- \u0060musoq data-sources import\u0060\n\n## Example\n\n### Import a reviewed local package\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060powershell\nmusoq data-sources import ./reviewed-plugin.zip --non-interactive --format json\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nExpected result: An installation outcome for an existing reviewed artifact. Import changes the active profile and may cause code to load; do not use an untrusted ZIP.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- The package is installed but its schema is absent. Inspect its enabled/reinstall status and dependency closure. Follow chapter 41; repeated installation is not evidence that activation succeeded.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nTreat the command help and generated contracts as authoritative for syntax. Datasource-specific SQL and plugin APIs are documented by their own versioned specifications.\n"
